From af533faba80318f6aec9eb41bc114cbafe2650ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:03:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(js-tests): admit workspace checks by memory as well as CPU
 [daveey]

A gw runner slot is 4 CPUs and 8 GiB with no swap. run-workspace-checks
started the first four units together, and those are the four
apps/desktop heavies (ui vitest, electron vitest, pack + packaged-app
tests, tsc + eslint); their measured peaks sum past 8 GiB. In runs
41009740205 and 41016178444 the kernel SIGKILLed tsc (exit 137) and the
vite build inside pack at the same instant.

Each package now declares the measured peak of its heavy units in a
package.json checkMemoryMiB map. A unit starts only when a CPU slot is
free and its peak fits in what the running units leave of the budget
(cgroup memory.max, else physical memory, less 1 GiB reserve). A unit
larger than the whole budget still runs, alone. A map key that names no
check unit is an error, so a renamed check cannot silently fall back to
the default. The summary prints the cgroup's memory.peak and oom_kill
so a later Killed says whether the memory limit did it.
